+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Product reviews currently expose the full customer representation publicly, accept invalid ratings, allow duplicate submissions to become server errors, and leave product aggregates stale after merchant changes. This harms privacy and makes review APIs unreliable and product ratings incorrect.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Return a privacy-safe public review DTO containing only review id, rating, description, date, and reviewer first name.
+- Validate customer review ratings as whole numbers from 1 through 5 and return 400 for invalid requests.
+- Enforce that the authenticated customer owns the submitted customer id, and return 403 when it does not.
+- Return 409 for a customer's second review of the same product without persisting it.
+- Make merchant update and delete operations address reviews by both product and review id, returning 404 for missing or mismatched reviews.
+- Recalculate product average rating and count from the complete review set after create, update, and delete, using one decimal place with half-up rounding and zero values when empty.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `product-reviews`: Public review privacy, customer submission rules, merchant review management, and product rating aggregation.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The v1 product review controller and request/response models, product review service and repository, review populators/facades, and product read mappers are affected. Integration and service tests should cover privacy, validation, authorization, duplicate conflict, product scoping, and aggregate recalculation.
